'''vulgarly''' (vul′gär-li), ''adv.'' '''1.''' In a vulgar manner; commonly; popularly; in the manner usual among the common people.
{{smaller block|The cleere gaines of those metals, the Kings part defraied, to the Aduenturers is but small, and nothing neere so much as ''vulgarly'' is imagined.
