'''2†.''' By or before the people; publicly.
{{smaller block|<poem>To justify this worthy nobleman,
So ''vulgarly'' and personally accused.</poem>
{{right|''Shak.'', M. for M., v. 1. 160.}}}}
'''3.''' Coarsely; rudely; clownishly.

'''vulgarness''' (vul′gär-nes), ''n.'' The state or character of being vulgar; vulgarity.

