'''vulned''' (vulnd), ''a.'' [< ''vuln'' + ''-ed''<sup>2</sup>.] In ''her.'', wounded: noting any animal used as a bearing, the weapon which inflicts the wound being generally mentioned. {{smaller|Frequently, however, ''vulned'' refers to the bleeding of the wound: thus, the blazon may be ''pierced by an arrow and vulned''.}}

