'''vulnerate†''' (vul′ne̤-rāt), ''v. t.'' [< L. ''vulneratus'', pp. of ''vulnerare'' (> It. ''vulnerare'' = Sp. Pg. ''vulnerar'' = OF. *''vulnerer''), wound, injure, < ''vulnus'' (''vulner-''), a wound; cf. Skt. ''vrana'', a wound, fracture; prob. from the root of ''vellere'', perf. ''vulsi'', pluck, tear: see ''vulture''.] To wound; hurt; injure.

